# Auto commit & push

After finishing code changes in this repo:

1. Commit with a concise message that focuses on why
2. Push to `origin` on the current branch

Do this by default — do not wait for the user to say "push" or "commit".

Skip only when:
- The user explicitly says not to commit or push
- There is nothing to commit
- Secrets or credentials would be included

Follow the existing git safety protocol (no force push to main/master, no config changes, no skipping hooks, HEREDOC commit messages).
